      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested** — Please expand the unit test in `zephyr/test/fpmcu/tests/bloonchipper/src/ec_quirks.c` to cover `sys_clock_disable()` and the updated `HOOK_SYSJUMP` behavior.\n\n### Review Summary\n* **Functionality:** ✅ Moving `st_stm32_timers`, `st_stm32_uart`, and `sys_clock_disable()` teardown from `HOOK_SYSJUMP` into `chip_pre_system_jump()` ensures peripheral and system clock teardown occurs after `watchdog_reload()` in `jump_to_image()`.\n* **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit:** ✅ Overrides `chip_pre_system_jump()` declared in `include/system.h`, matching the system jump teardown lifecycle.\n* **Code Simplicity:** ✅ The split between `chip_pre_system_jump()` and `prepare_for_sysjump_to_ec()` is minimal and direct.\n* **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:** ✅ Follows ChromiumOS EC / Zephyr conventions with no magic values.\n* **Security:** ✅ No security issues introduced; MPU teardown remains in place prior to jumping to the target image.\n* **Testing:** ❌ `test_chip_pre_system_jump` only checks `stm32_reset_line_toggle` and does not verify that `chip_pre_system_jump()` calls `sys_clock_disable()` or that `HOOK_SYSJUMP` (`prepare_for_sysjump_to_ec()`) calls `arm_core_mpu_disable()` without tearing down peripherals/clocks early. See inline comment.\n* **CL Size \u0026 Scope:** ✅ `Size: S (+25, -7)` — Focused, single logical change (+12, -7 production lines; +13, -0 test lines).\n* **Commit Message:** ✅ Clear, accurate summary and rationale with proper `BUG\u003d` and `TEST\u003d` tags.\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/5c3a5228-9188-49db-bb42-c732d99b76b9)",
