      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] `test_chip_pre_system_jump` only verifies that `timers2` is reset, leaving two parts of this change untested:\n\n1. `chip_pre_system_jump()` also calls `sys_clock_disable()`, which is not faked or asserted here (if `sys_clock_disable()` were removed, the test would still pass). Since `sys_clock_disable()` has a weak default implementation on `native_sim`, it can be faked with `FAKE_VOID_FUNC(sys_clock_disable)`.\n2. `prepare_for_sysjump_to_ec()` (`HOOK_SYSJUMP`) was modified in this CL to only call `arm_core_mpu_disable()` and no longer reset peripherals or disable the system clock. `FAKE_VOID_FUNC(arm_core_mpu_disable)` and `hooks.h` are already present in this file, so we can directly test `hook_notify(HOOK_SYSJUMP)` as well.\n\nPlease add a fake for `sys_clock_disable` (with `#include \u003czephyr/drivers/timer/system_timer.h\u003e`) and verify both `chip_pre_system_jump()` and `HOOK_SYSJUMP`:\n\n```c\nZTEST(ec_quirks, test_chip_pre_system_jump)\n{\n\tRESET_FAKE(arm_core_mpu_disable);\n\tRESET_FAKE(stm32_reset_line_toggle);\n\tRESET_FAKE(sys_clock_disable);\n\n\tchip_pre_system_jump();\n\n\tzassert_equal(stm32_reset_line_toggle_fake.call_count, 1);\n\tzassert_equal(stm32_reset_line_toggle_fake.arg0_history[0],\n\t\t      DEVICE_DT_GET(DT_NODELABEL(rctl)));\n\tzassert_equal(stm32_reset_line_toggle_fake.arg1_history[0],\n\t\t      DT_RESET_ID(DT_NODELABEL(timers2)));\n\tzassert_equal(sys_clock_disable_fake.call_count, 1);\n\tzassert_equal(arm_core_mpu_disable_fake.call_count, 0);\n}\n\nZTEST(ec_quirks, test_prepare_for_sysjump_to_ec)\n{\n\tRESET_FAKE(arm_core_mpu_disable);\n\tRESET_FAKE(stm32_reset_line_toggle);\n\tRESET_FAKE(sys_clock_disable);\n\n\thook_notify(HOOK_SYSJUMP);\n\n\tzassert_equal(arm_core_mpu_disable_fake.call_count, 1);\n\tzassert_equal(stm32_reset_line_toggle_fake.call_count, 0);\n\tzassert_equal(sys_clock_disable_fake.call_count, 0);\n}\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/5c3a5228-9188-49db-bb42-c732d99b76b9)",
